    "title": "Small earthquake recorded in northwest Kansas - NewsBreak",
    "text": "13 hours ago It happened shortly after 7:30 a.m., according to the U.S. Geological Survey. The temblor was centered just off U.S. Highway 24, west of Webster State Lake, in Rooks County, underneath a field near an oil well. The quake measured 2.5 in magnitude and had a depth of around 6.2 miles.... Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak 9",
